他将自己犯下的强奸罪归咎于“梦魇”。杜托伊的妻子娜塔莉站在丈夫一边，并出庭支持他。他将妻子的忠诚归功于他施下的咒语，要求她永远没有离开他的能力。1992年，南非警察局成立了一个专门处理邪教相关犯罪的部门，以应对当时席卷全国的“撒旦恐慌”。“撒旦恐慌”是20世纪末在全球范围内蔓延的一种道德恐慌，但在南非尤为严重，因为那里对神秘学的信仰根深蒂固。邪教犯罪部门的一名警官在审判中发言，驳斥了杜托伊关于恶魔附身的说法。他说，杜托伊对自己罪行的清晰回忆意味着他完全能够控制自己的行为。该警官还声称，如果杜托伊真的被附身，他也会强奸自己的妻子，但他并没有这样做。

50
00:49:43.000 --> 00:50:55.000
While Dutoy seemed to enjoy the limelight and his newfound notoriety, Tian's Kruger was quieter. A clinical psychologist who had examined Kruger determined that the 19-year-old had borderline personality disorder and suffered from extremely low self-esteem. Franz Dutoy and Tian's Kruger were ultimately convicted of two counts of rape, two charges of indecent assault, two counts of abduction, attempted murder, and theft. During sentencing, the judge dismissed Dutoy's claims of demonic possession and sentenced him to three terms of life imprisonment. Kruger was given one count of life imprisonment for the crimes against Allison, plus 25 years for the second rape. The judge made it clear that while Kruger may have been influenced by his older accomplice, he still exhibited disturbing bloodlust. The judge concluded with one final decree, quote, I also make the following order.
虽然杜托伊似乎很享受聚光灯和新获得的恶名，但蒂安·克鲁格则安静得多。一名为克鲁格做过检查的临床心理学家确定，这名19岁的年轻人患有边缘性人格障碍，且自尊心极低。弗朗茨·杜托伊和蒂安·克鲁格最终被判犯有两项强奸罪、两项猥亵罪、两项绑架罪、谋杀未遂罪和盗窃罪。在量刑时，法官驳回了杜托伊关于恶魔附身的说法，判处他三次终身监禁。克鲁格因对艾莉森的罪行被判处一次终身监禁，外加因第二起强奸案被判25年监禁。法官明确表示，虽然克鲁格可能受到了他年长同伙的影响，但他仍然表现出了令人不安的嗜血本性。法官最后做出了最后的一项裁决，引用如下：“我还做出以下命令。”

51
00:50:55.000 --> 00:52:07.000
It must be clear that if at any time in the future there is any consideration for parole, it was my intention that these two men be removed from society for the rest of their natural lives, and that they should spend it behind bars. Cheers echoed through the courtroom in response to the judge's words. As Dutoy and Kruger were being escorted out, Kruger slammed his hand against the wall and shouted, Here we go. Fuck you all. With both men convicted and sentenced, Allison was free to speak publicly about her ordeal. She was eager to do so in the hopes that her words might inspire other women who had been raped to come forward. Allison knew that many rape survivors were left with a feeling of shame and wanted to make it clear that they had nothing to be ashamed of. Allison gave an exclusive interview to a magazine titled You and also spoke on air with a local radio presenter.
必须明确的是，如果未来任何时候考虑假释，我的意图是让这两个人余生都与社会隔绝，在监狱中度过。法庭上回荡着对法官这番话的欢呼声。当杜托伊和克鲁格被押送出去时，克鲁格猛地拍了一下墙壁，大喊道：走着瞧。去你们的。随着两人被定罪判刑，艾莉森终于可以公开谈论她的遭遇了。她渴望这样做，希望自己的话能激励其他被强奸的女性勇敢站出来。艾莉森知道，许多强奸幸存者都背负着羞耻感，她想明确表示，她们没有什么可羞耻的。艾莉森接受了《You》杂志的独家采访，并与当地的一位电台主持人进行了连线。

52
00:52:07.000 --> 00:53:13.000
When the male presenter told her he felt honored to speak with a rape survivor as he had never done so before, Allison responded, You don't know that. So many women are silent about it. At the same time that she was publicly advocating for survivors of rape, Allison was also going through a gruelling recovery. Even as her physical wounds began to heal, she was left with significant scarring that required reconstructive and plastic surgery. Too scared to return to the apartment where she'd been living at the time of the attack, Allison moved to a new one in a more secure complex. She also struggled with focusing at work and soon sank into a deep depression. One day, Allison received an invitation to give a talk about her experiences at a rotary club. Although public speaking made her nervous, she decided to accept the offer.
当男主持人告诉她，他很荣幸能与一位强奸幸存者交谈，因为他以前从未这样做过时，艾莉森回答说：你不知道这一点。有太多的女性对此保持沉默。在公开为强奸幸存者倡导的同时，艾莉森也正在经历一段极其痛苦的康复过程。即使她的身体伤口开始愈合，她仍留下了严重的疤痕，需要进行重建和整形手术。由于害怕回到袭击发生时居住的公寓，艾莉森搬到了一个安保设施更好的新公寓。她还难以集中精力工作，很快陷入了深深的抑郁之中。一天，艾莉森收到邀请，去扶轮社讲述她的经历。尽管公开演讲让她感到紧张，但她还是决定接受邀请。

53
00:53:13.000 --> 00:54:20.000
To her surprise, the talk went well. Soon she was accepting more opportunities to speak at other events. Allison found that speaking publicly about her attack helped her come to terms with it. Because she had to tell audiences what she had learnt through it all, she began to reflect more deeply on how she had survived. Encouraged by the positive feedback she received from those who attended her talks, Allison eventually embarked on a career as a motivational speaker. She won multiple awards for her bravery and would wind up travelling all over the world to share her story. When she married, she took her husband's surname of Buerta and became known by this name in the media. Allison also worked with author Marianne Tham to write a book about her experiences. It was published in 1998 under the title I Have Life.
令她惊讶的是，演讲进行得很顺利。很快，她接受了更多在其他活动中演讲的机会。艾莉森发现，公开谈论她的袭击经历有助于她接受这一切。因为她必须告诉听众她从中领悟到了什么，她开始更深刻地反思自己是如何幸存下来的。在听众给予的积极反馈的鼓励下，艾莉森最终开启了励志演说家的职业生涯。她因勇敢而赢得了多个奖项，并最终前往世界各地分享她的故事。结婚后，她随了丈夫的姓氏布尔塔，并以这个名字在媒体上为人所知。艾莉森还与作家玛丽安·塔姆合作写了一本关于她经历的书。该书于1998年以《我拥有生命》为题出版。

54
00:54:20.000 --> 00:55:12.000
In 2011, new legislation came into force in South Africa, which meant all prisoners who had been given life sentences prior to 2004 could apply for parole, providing they had already served at least 13 years and 4 months. Franz Dutoy and Tianz Kruger both fell under this category. The two applied for parole. Kruger appeared before his prison's parole board in December 2011 and was said to have boasted to fellow inmates that he would soon be free. Dutoy had his hearing the following month. Authorities did not notify Allison or the pair's other victims of this development and they were left to learn about the man's possible release via the media.
2011年，南非实施了新立法，这意味着所有在2004年之前被判终身监禁的囚犯，只要已经服刑至少13年零4个月，就可以申请假释。弗朗茨·杜托伊和蒂安兹·克鲁格都属于这一类。两人都申请了假释。克鲁格于2011年12月出现在监狱假释委员会面前，据称他向狱友吹嘘自己很快就会重获自由。杜托伊在次月进行了听证会。当局没有通知艾莉森或这两人的其他受害者这一进展，他们只能通过媒体得知这两人可能获释的消息。

55
00:55:12.000 --> 00:56:15.000
Allison was devastated. She believed that the judge's order at sentencing meant her attackers would never be freed. To her relief, neither man was given parole, but they were still permitted to reapply for it every two years. In August of 2015, Allison, who was now 47 years old, received a strange email from an American woman named Joyce. She was getting in touch with Allison because she was worried about her daughter Sabrina, who was 34. According to Joyce, Sabrina was engaged to Franz Dutoy, now aged 46, and wanted to travel to South Africa to help him with his next parole application. The pair had met via Facebook and communicated entirely online. Sabrina hadn't initially known that Dutoy was in prison.
艾莉森感到崩溃。她认为法官在判刑时的命令意味着她的袭击者永远不会被释放。令她欣慰的是，两人都没有获得假释，但他们仍被允许每两年重新申请一次。2015年8月，当时47岁的艾莉森收到了一位名叫乔伊斯的美国女性发来的奇怪邮件。她联系艾莉森是因为她担心自己34岁的女儿萨布丽娜。据乔伊斯说，萨布丽娜与现年46岁的弗朗茨·杜托伊订了婚，并想去南非帮助他进行下一次假释申请。两人通过Facebook相识，完全在网上交流。萨布丽娜起初并不知道杜托伊在坐牢。

56
00:56:15.000 --> 00:57:24.000
When he told her what he was serving time for, Dutoy admitted to being a rapist but claimed he had no part in trying to kill Allison. That attack was entirely the fault of his accomplice, Tianz Kruger. He also said that the prison authorities were pleased with his progress and believed he was a changed man. When Sabrina's mother, Joyce, found out about the relationship, she contacted South Africa's Department of Correctional Services, but received no response. So she decided to reach out to Dutoy's soul-named victim, Allison Buerta. Joyce attached page after page of correspondence between Sabrina and Dutoy, which she'd obtained from her daughter's Facebook account. In his writings to Sabrina, Dutoy claimed that he'd organized for a woman to be raped after she accused him of killing her father. He'd also had another woman gang-raped by some men he called his boys.
当他告诉她他因何入狱时，杜托伊承认自己是强奸犯，但声称他没有参与谋杀艾莉森的企图。那次袭击完全是他同伙蒂安兹·克鲁格的错。他还说，监狱当局对他的表现很满意，认为他已经改过自新。当萨布丽娜的母亲乔伊斯发现这段关系时，她联系了南非惩教署，但没有得到回应。于是她决定联系杜托伊的受害者艾莉森·布尔塔。乔伊斯附上了萨布丽娜和杜托伊之间的大量通信记录，这些记录是她从女儿的Facebook账户中获取的。在写给萨布丽娜的信中，杜托伊声称他曾组织人强奸了一名指控他杀害其父亲的女性。他还让其他女性被他称之为“我的男孩们”的一群人轮奸。

57
00:57:24.000 --> 00:58:31.000
Dutoy said he'd done all of this from behind bars. He made threats against people he wanted to harm when he was released and asked Sabrina for money. Dutoy also bragged about how he'd bribed prison officials into letting him have access to mobile phones. Allison was horrified and couldn't believe Dutoy was being allowed access to social media. She emailed a complaint to prison authorities who in turn forwarded it to Dutoy. Angered by the lack of regard being shown for her personal safety, Allison went to the media for help. Despite articles being published in the magazine You and Other Publications, Dutoy was still allowed to maintain multiple Facebook accounts. When Franz Dutoy heard that a South African film director named Uga Carlini was making a feature documentary about the attack against Allison and her survival,
杜托伊说，这一切都是他在狱中完成的。他威胁要伤害那些他出狱后想报复的人，并向萨布丽娜要钱。杜托伊还吹嘘自己如何贿赂监狱官员，让他们允许他使用手机。艾莉森感到震惊，无法相信杜托伊竟然被允许使用社交媒体。她向监狱当局发送了投诉邮件，当局随后将其转发给了杜托伊。由于对个人安全缺乏重视感到愤怒，艾莉森向媒体寻求帮助。尽管《You》杂志和其他出版物发表了相关文章，但杜托伊仍然被允许保留多个Facebook账户。当弗朗茨·杜托伊听说南非电影导演乌加·卡里尼正在制作一部关于艾莉森遇袭及其幸存经历的纪录片时，

58
00:58:31.000 --> 00:59:31.000
he reached out and offered to be interviewed. But he made it clear that he had some conditions. First, he wanted a signed letter from Allison Werther saying that she had forgiven him. And second, he demanded a backdated share of the profits from Allison's motivational speaking career and book sales as he said she owed all of her success to his actions. Uga Carlini refused Dutoy's request. Her documentary titled Allison was released in 2016. Allison Werther's life wasn't the only one changed by what happened to her on December 17, 1994. Tiana Eilard, the man who helped save Allison by providing first aid, was so affected by the incident that he decided to become a doctor instead of a vet.
他主动联系并提出接受采访。但他明确表示自己有一些条件。首先，他想要一封艾莉森·布尔塔签署的信，说明她已经原谅了他。其次，他要求获得艾莉森励志演讲生涯和书籍销售利润的追溯分成，因为他说她的成功全归功于他的行为。乌加·卡里尼拒绝了杜托伊的要求。她的纪录片《艾莉森》于2016年上映。艾莉森·布尔塔的生活并不是1994年12月17日发生的事情中唯一被改变的。通过提供急救帮助挽救艾莉森的蒂安娜·埃拉德，深受此事影响，决定成为一名医生而不是兽医。

59
00:59:31.000 --> 01:00:44.000
He and Allison have remained close throughout the years and in November 2006, when Allison gave birth to her second child, Tiana assisted with the delivery. Becoming a mother felt like a miracle to Allison. She was worried that she would never be able to have children due to the injuries she sustained during the attack, but she now has two sons. After Allison Werther's two attackers were convicted, she was given a small cardboard box filled with evidence that police had gathered from the crime scene. It contained her clothing and other personal belongings that had been dumped on the ground. For a long time, Allison kept the box at the back of a cupboard and refused to look inside. But a few years later, while working on her book with author Marianne Timm, she decided to do something with it. As described in the book I Have Life, Allison, Marianne and Allison's husband took the box back to the location where Allison was almost killed.
多年来，他和艾莉森一直保持着密切联系。2006年11月，当艾莉森生下第二个孩子时，蒂安娜协助了分娩。对艾莉森来说，成为母亲感觉就像一个奇迹。她曾担心由于袭击中受到的伤害，自己可能永远无法生育，但她现在有两个儿子。在艾莉森·布尔塔的两名袭击者被定罪后，她收到了一个装满警察从犯罪现场收集的证据的小纸箱。里面装着她的衣服和其他被扔在地上的个人物品。很长一段时间里，艾莉森把这个盒子放在橱柜后面，拒绝看里面的东西。但几年后，在与作家玛丽安·蒂姆合作写书时，她决定处理一下这些东西。正如书《我拥有生命》中所述，艾莉森、玛丽安和艾莉森的丈夫把盒子带回了艾莉森差点丧命的地方。

